{"chunk_id": "52ceac3f1d57", "text": "This section depicts the climactic struggle between Lakshmana and Indrajit during the war in Lanka. After Angada destroys Indrajit\u2019s chariot with a hurled tree, the Rakshasa prince turns invisible and devastates the battlefield with divine arrows, binding Rama and Lakshmana in a deadly net. The monkey army gathers in despair until Vibhishana revives the brothers and provides sacred water from Kuvera that allows them to see invisible foes. When Indrajit returns to battle before completing his sacrificial rites, Lakshmana confronts him. In a decisive duel, Lakshmana severs Indrajit\u2019s arms and finally his head with three blazing arrows. The victory breaks Ravana\u2019s greatest military advantage, but the grief-stricken demon king, maddened by loss, nearly turns his fury upon the captive Sita.\nIndrajit briefly incapacitates Rama and Lakshmana with enchanted arrows, but after recovery Lakshmana duels and kills him, plunging Ravana into grief.\nThemes: heroic duel, illusion in warfare, divine weapons, loyal allies, vengeance and grief", "vector": [0.0031690718606114388, -0.018228044733405113, -0.005860934499651194, 0.00860992819070816, -0.0016693917568773031, 0.009201398119330406, -0.027046330273151398, -0.02922401763498783, -0.026226337999105453, -0.023416852578520775, 0.015741178765892982, 0.01871197484433651, 0.010330568999052048, 0.006791828200221062, 0.0019021151820197701, 0.014974956400692463, 0.040461957454681396, -0.020728351548314095, 0.034117091447114944, -0.008757795207202435, -0.020244421437382698, 0.003436241764575243, -0.003505134489387274, 0.010377617552876472, -0.024667005985975266, 0.0018248207634314895, 0.013287921436131, -0.0396285206079483, 0.018953939899802208, -0.008139439858496189, -0.01123793888837099, -0.01873886026442051, -0.004066359251737595, -0.011264823377132416, -0.03250398859381676, -0.010532206855714321, -0.0036126745399087667, -0.014275945723056793, 0.012851039879024029, 0.0007851266418583